course: dictionary
lesson: 9242
title: The highest voice
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A soprano is the highest singing voice. In a choir, the sopranos sing the top line, and a soprano can be a woman, a girl, or a boy before his voice breaks. «In the 1990s scientists noticed some pipistrelles called at a higher pitch than others.» Pitch means how high or low a sound is, so the higher calls are the ones to look for.
explain: The clues in a sentence can help you. «They were two kinds, the common and the soprano pipistrelle.» The word sits next to common, so it names a different kind. The scientists chose the name because the bat's calls were high. When you see soprano, ask: is this about a singer, or about something high?
explain: Soprano can also be an adjective, a describing word, for instruments. A soprano recorder is in the highest range of the recorder family. Your school recorder is usually a soprano recorder, so you may already play one.
fact: A soprano is the highest singing voice.
fact: In a choir, the voices are grouped as soprano, alto, tenor and bass.
fact: Children's school recorders are usually soprano recorders.
fact: Phrases to know: «soprano part», «soprano line», «boy soprano», «sing soprano».
fact: «Soprano» can also name a singer, and it can describe an instrument in the highest range of its family.
exercise: In a choir, which voice sings the highest notes? | Bass | Tenor | *Soprano | Alto
exercise: «In the 1990s scientists noticed some pipistrelles called at a higher pitch than others; studies showed they were two kinds, the common and the soprano pipistrelle.» Find and copy the word that names the higher-pitched kind. | scientists | common | studies | *soprano
exercise: What is a soprano recorder? | A recorder with no holes | A recorder in the lowest range of its family | A recorder made only of wood | *A recorder in the highest range of its family
test: What is a boy soprano? | A boy with a deep bass voice | A boy who whispers all his songs | *A boy who sings in the highest voice, before his voice breaks | A boy who plays the drums
test: Priya says, «The soprano part is for the lowest singers.» What is wrong with her idea? | *The soprano part is the highest part, not the lowest | Soprano only means a recorder | Nothing, she is right | Soprano means the same as bass, so she is right
exam: Mia's school choir needs a singer for the top line, which sings the highest notes. Which voice part should she sing? | Tenor | *Soprano | Alto | Bass
